{"kind":"request","text":"GS-3: the scale tier selects two groups, so a kernel head does not\nrun the older six cases.\n\nThis request answers audit `de28ac2b` for request `117bdb74`. It rules\nagainst selection for each owner and for a smaller change.\n\nThe numbers:\n\n- The C2 gate omitted scale, and its Native stage took 590 s (END\n  `78005ded`). The GS-1 gate ran all 22 cases in 1,338 s. Those are\n  two heads, so the difference is an observation and not a saving.\n- After GS-1, an edit of `packages/derive/src/judge.ts` selects all 13\n  owners and 22 cases. Before GS-1, that edit ran the moved sixteen as\n  ordinary cases and omitted the older six. E1 pays for that change.\n- The audit's case sums: the older six take 974 s and the moved\n  sixteen take 643 s.\n- Selection for each owner does not help E1. The five common runtime\n  paths reach all 13 owners.\n\nThe change:\n\n1. The selector answers `omit`, `moved` or `all`.\n2. The older six cases, in their four owners, follow the selection\n   rule of main `270dc8c7`, the rule before GS-1. A path that selected\n   them then selects `all` now.\n3. The moved sixteen cases, in their nine owners, follow the protected\n   paths of GS-1. A path that only GS-1 protects selects `moved`.\n4. A change of the selector, of the scale configuration or of the\n   count inventory selects `all`. Main and the daily run select `all`.\n5. The runner takes its expected owners and its case count from the\n   selected group. It refuses an unknown answer, a missing owner, an\n   extra owner and a wrong count. An `omit` answer reports no scale\n   result.\n6. `docs/testing.md` states the three answers.\n\nThe coverage of a kernel head returns to what it was before GS-1: the\nsixteen run, and the older six run on main each day.\n\nThe first gate that selects `moved` reports its Native wall time. That\nnumber decides whether the rule stays.\n\nOrder: the head changes the selector, so its own gate runs all 22. It\ncan ride with FH-1 (`c8b2f4f6`) as one tooling head under one gate. It\ndoes not go ahead of NF-5, C2 or C3. You choose its place relative to\nE1.\n\nThis request adds no scope kind, no platform definition name, no\ncapability name or form, no tool family and no record model.","body":{"conditions":"An edit of packages/derive/src/judge.ts alone selects the moved sixteen cases and omits the older six, a path that selected the older six at main 270dc8c7 selects all 22, the runner refuses a wrong owner set or count for the selected group, and docs/testing.md states the three answers.","target_head":"336dd74e990f057834ac8b2edc92a4287315ec8c","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}